    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that participant experience is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_6ec240b0d0472b51\",\"quote\":\"For example, it sometimes finds us when we are still energetic.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"The evidence does not support a causal link between institutional procedures and participant experience.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim oversimplifies the complex factors influencing participant experience, ignoring other potential drivers.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The evidence suggests factors like family dynamics, government policies, and individual perceptions are also significant.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The provided sources primarily detail frustrations with government policies, food consumption, and personal anxieties related to the pandemic, not a primary driver of experience through institutional procedures. \"}",
